{"ok": false, "issues": ["The requirement runs to about ten sentences and needs condensing to 1-2 plain sentences. Its substance matches the § 15B excerpts: the 1-month cap, a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account with a receipt within 30 days, 5%/yr interest (or the lesser bank rate) when the deposit is held 1 year or longer, return within 30 days less permitted deductions with a sworn itemized damage list, and the fee-in-lieu authority effective Aug 1, 2025 under St. 2025, c. 9.", "Status in_force, subject landlord, null coverage_logic, yields_to_local/preempts_local false, effective_date null (long-standing statute) and citation M.G.L. c. 186, § 15B are all correct. The deposit cap is in § 15B(1)(b)(iii), but the record covers the whole section, so the section-level citation stays."], "scope": "core", "applies_only_in": [], "conflict_unresolved": false, "conflict_note": null, "fix": {"requirement": "A landlord may not take a security deposit larger than the first month's rent and must hold it in a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account, give the tenant a receipt naming the bank, amount and account number within 30 days, and, if it holds the deposit for 1 year or longer, pay interest at 5% per year (or the lesser rate the bank paid) each year of the tenancy. Within 30 days after the tenancy ends, the landlord must return the deposit, deducting only unpaid rent or water charges, unpaid tax-escalation amounts, or reasonable repair costs for damage beyond normal wear and tear, which must be supported by a sworn itemized list with cost evidence; since Aug 1, 2025, state regulations may allow an optional fee in lieu of a deposit, capped at 1 month's rent."}}
